Z||000000||skptrcr007||05-15-2001||12:15 AM||||I have an opportunity to buy a 85 GT that has a plate on the console between the seats that says that it was driven down the assembly line twice and that this was sponsored by General Motors. Does anyone have info on this, like did it really happen, is this for real or what..Thank you||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-15-2001||01:32 AM||||I don't remember exactly when it was but there was a large Fiero show (sponsered by FOCOA or FOA and GM) That had all the Fiero's drive down the assembly line (a second time, First time was when they were built). I remember I was going to go but I couldn't make it. I know a few folks in our local club that have the same plate. Yes it really happened. I think the time frame was 1989/1990.||||reg||1
Z||000002||skptrcr007||05-15-2001||01:45 PM||||Does this add value to the vehicle? Should I buy?<P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Oreif||05-15-2001||06:52 PM||||It doesn't add value, It's just one of those trivia things to boast about. What is the condition of the car and the price? If you tells us condition, options, mileage and such we can give you an average value for the car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Stoic||05-15-2001||08:04 PM||||You guys amaze me sometimes.  I consider myself to be fairly knowledgeable when it comes to fieros, yet members often spew out these facts that I have never heard.  Never the less, an interesting fact.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||05-15-2001||08:41 PM||||According to Chris Shaffer in the most recent edition of FOCONE publication, this event happend at the 3rd annual FOCOA show held in Pontiac Michigan in 1987.  This was the first show Chris attended.||||reg||6
